From: OneEmu build <hyungjun@neptunecompany.kr>
Subject: [PATCH] common/error: use the GNU strerror_r on every Android build

NDK clang++ predefines _GNU_SOURCE, so bionic's strerror_r returns
`char*` (GNU flavour) regardless of HAVE_LIBRETRO.  Upstream only takes
the GNU branch when `ANDROID && !HAVE_LIBRETRO`, so the libretro core
falls into the XSI branch and fails to compile on bionic:

  error: cannot initialize a variable of type 'int' with an rvalue of type 'char *'

Take the GNU branch on Android unconditionally.

diff --git a/src/common/error.cpp b/src/common/error.cpp
--- a/src/common/error.cpp
+++ b/src/common/error.cpp
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ std::string NativeErrorToString(int e) {
 #else
     char err_str[255];
 #if defined(__GLIBC__) && (_GNU_SOURCE || (_POSIX_C_SOURCE < 200112L && _XOPEN_SOURCE < 600)) ||   \
-    (defined(ANDROID) && !defined(HAVE_LIBRETRO))
+    defined(ANDROID)
     // Thread safe (GNU-specific)
     const char* str = strerror_r(e, err_str, sizeof(err_str));
     return std::string(str);
